<%# Body copy lives in config/locales/ru.yml and en.yml under
    notification_mailer.welcome_letter.body -- see NotificationMailer for
    why the mail is rendered in the recipient's locale, not the sender's.

    The host var below replaces the "bien.kg" that was hardcoded into the
    Merb-era version of this template: encounter-engine is meant to be
    installed by anyone on their own domain (see README.md), so naming one
    specific installation's domain in every deployment's mail was a bug,
    not a feature. Defaults to "bien.kg" so existing deployments see no
    change; override per-instance with APP_HOST, alongside this app's
    other per-instance ENV overrides (TZ, DEFAULT_LOCALE -- see
    config/application.rb). %>
<%= t("notification_mailer.welcome_letter.body",
      host: ENV.fetch("APP_HOST", "bien.kg"),
      email: @user.email,
      password: @password) %>
